# a2a-switchboard — environment template
#
# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in real values. NEVER commit real
# secrets to this repository — CI runs gitleaks on every push and PR.
#
# The switchboard does not read .env itself; these variables are consumed by
# docker-compose / systemd overrides:
#   AGW_BIND          listen address (default 127.0.0.1:9920)
#   AGW_DATA_DIR      state directory (default ./data — holds state.json with
#                     the gateway/bootstrap tokens; keep it out of git too)
#   AGW_HEARTBEAT_SEC peer health probe interval (default 30)
#   AGW_COOKIE_SECURE     set 1 when a TLS terminator fronts the gateway —
#                         session cookies get the Secure flag
#   AGW_ROUTING_LOG_MAX_MB  routing.jsonl cap before rotation (default 64;
#                           0 disables the on-disk audit log)
#   AGW_AUDIT_PREVIEWS     false to drop redacted request previews from the
#                          audit log (free-text parts can hold secrets)
#
# Gateway tokens (agw_...) live in data/state.json on the gateway host and are
# minted on first run — there is nothing to pre-configure here. The admin UI
# password is likewise generated on first run and printed to the logs once.
#
# Per-peer secrets used by Hermes clients (caller_token / upstream_token in
# ~/.hermes/config.yaml) must be generated per peer and distributed out of
# band. See docs/integrations/hermes.md.
AGW_BIND=127.0.0.1:9920
AGW_DATA_DIR=./data
AGW_HEARTBEAT_SEC=30
#AGW_COOKIE_SECURE=1
#AGW_ROUTING_LOG_MAX_MB=64
#AGW_AUDIT_PREVIEWS=true
